  "idea": "How to schedule emails to send at a later date and time automatically",
  "text": "If you write work emails late on Sunday night, do not send them right now. Midnight messages train demanding clients to expect instant replies, destroying your personal boundaries. Furthermore, late emails get buried underneath hundreds of morning newsletters before your recipient logs on. Click the dropdown arrow next to Send in Gmail or Outlook and select Schedule Send instead. Your message lands at nine Monday morning with zero stress.",
